</blockquote>
<p>Is this supposed to be as funny as it is? I get what happened and why it should be considered horrifying, but this line almost makes it come off as satire. It'd be a +1 from me except&#8230;</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The satire almost doesn't work for me if I'm understanding why the area that causes the effect is 15m x 60m. The implication is that it's a statue that's part of the indigenous culture there or something, right? Kinda plays into savage tropes, and that sorta takes away from the whole jab at colonialism.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>If I'm wrong, I'm wrong, and I'll change my vote; but, if I'm wrong, then the redacted portion of the image kind of seems arbitrary&#8230; Currently a no-vote.</p>

